WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.119 --> 00:00:05.443
- Here's a microphone.

00:00:05.443 --> 00:00:08.276
I'm gonna put this under your arm.

00:00:14.251 --> 00:00:15.084
- (Mark) All right, Kellie.

00:00:15.084 --> 00:00:16.140
Kellie, where'd you grow up?

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:16.973
Where are you from?

00:00:16.973 --> 00:00:18.750
- I grew up in Queens, New York.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.683
I was born in Brooklyn.

00:00:20.683 --> 00:00:22.270
- (Mark) And tell me about your childhood.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.020
You grew up with both of your parents?

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.450
- No, I grew up with just my mom.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.190
My dad was in federal prison.

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:29.573
I have four brothers and one sister.

00:00:29.573 --> 00:00:31.000
- (Mark) And how was your childhood?

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.820
- Oh. My childhood was um,

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.180
it wasn't a normal childhood.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.710
I had four brothers who
have had sex with me,

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.450
before I even knew what sex was.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.270
I've been in three mental institutions

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.653
before the age of eleven.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.900
I came to California at the age of 14.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.810
My father came to New York and got me.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:52.078
And from there I was
pregnant by my brother.

00:00:52.078 --> 00:00:53.740
- (Mark) So you had sex
with all of your brothers?

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.020
- All four of my brothers, ongoing.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.570
And I didn't tell anybody

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:01.610
because I was always like the black sheep

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:02.443
of the family,

00:01:02.443 --> 00:01:05.280
so me and my mom weren't close.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.840
She was close to her boys,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.890
and that's why I'm real tomboyish today.

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:12.280
So anyway, my father came and got me

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.840
at the age of 14

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.530
and brought me to California,

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:18.440
but I was pregnant by my brother.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.547
But I didn't know I was pregnant,

00:01:19.547 --> 00:01:21.340
and he didn't know I was pregnant.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:23.430
But I carried real small,

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.210
so I never told anybody I was pregnant,

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:28.300
and when he found out I was pregnant,

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.820
he left me in an apartment,

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.170
and the manager of the
apartment called the police,

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:35.020
'cause she would see me all the time,

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:36.680
and the police came and got me,

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.028
and I went to a foster home in Compton.

00:01:39.028 --> 00:01:40.150
- (Mark) At what age?

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:41.840
- I was 14 still.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.830
I went to a foster home in Compton.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:44.663
I had the baby.

00:01:44.663 --> 00:01:45.770
I don't know the baby,

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:47.800
but my foster father got me pregnant,

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.160
in the foster home.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.020
So I have a boy and a girl,

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.184
but I don't know either one of them.

00:01:53.184 --> 00:01:54.310
- (Mark) Wow.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:56.610
At what age did you start having sex?

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:59.130
- Oh. It was early on.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.330
I don't even know the age

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.870
because my brothers had started with me.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:04.850
I don't think they really
knew what they were doing,

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:07.490
but maybe they saw somebody doing it,

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.140
but it went on, and on, and on.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:10.880
One time I was like up here,

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.660
looking at my brother

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:13.710
on top of me in the basement.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:14.543
Yeah.

00:02:14.543 --> 00:02:18.020
But anyway, so I had the baby from

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.000
my foster father.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.300
I had a girl.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.080
And the little girl actually went

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:26.510
to the foster home that I was in.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:30.160
So actually her dad was the foster father,

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.080
but no one knew,

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.250
because we never told anyone.

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:36.850
And from there I went
to another foster home.

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.670
They tried to take me to a group home,

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:39.910
I ran away,

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:41.730
and I just kinda been like,

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.050
on my own since then you know,

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:45.970
doing what I need to do.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:46.860
Just to get by.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.370
I've been homeless for 15 years.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:54.037
Now I have-- they got
me in an SRO over here.

00:02:54.037 --> 00:02:54.870
- (Mark) That's awesome.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:58.840
- And um, that's about how it goes.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.690
You know I've done just what I had to do

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:01.523
to get by.

00:03:01.523 --> 00:03:03.750
I've had drug addictions, you know.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.190
But, I've had syphilis,

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.580
I've had dis-- you know.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:10.315
But I just make it the
best way I can make it.

00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:11.780
- (Mark) Yeah.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:12.867
And how old are you now?

00:03:12.867 --> 00:03:14.138
- I'm 56 years old.

00:03:14.138 --> 00:03:14.971
- (Mark) 56?

00:03:14.971 --> 00:03:15.804
- Yes.

00:03:15.804 --> 00:03:17.690
- (Mark) And you have two
children, but you don't --

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:18.523
- I don't know them.

00:03:18.523 --> 00:03:19.356
- (Mark) You don't know them.

00:03:19.356 --> 00:03:20.189
- Yeah.

00:03:20.189 --> 00:03:23.390
They are like thirty-something.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:27.310
The oldest one might be like 38, 36 maybe?

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:31.792
He was born in '77, and
one was born in '78-- '79.

00:03:31.792 --> 00:03:33.000
- (Mark) Have you ever--

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:33.880
- Tried to pursue?

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.163
No, no.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:37.513
Because my life is not,

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.420
I mean it wasn't together then,

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.226
and it's really not together now.

00:03:42.226 --> 00:03:43.320
- (Mark) Has it ever been?

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.153
- No.

00:03:44.153 --> 00:03:46.510
Well, for two years it was.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:47.392
For two years.

00:03:47.392 --> 00:03:48.225
- (Mark) Tell me about those two years.

00:03:48.225 --> 00:03:49.570
- I went through a drug program,

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:50.800
the Rena B.,

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:53.783
and I stayed sober for two years.

00:03:53.783 --> 00:03:55.810
- (Mark) And how was that?

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.430
- That two years was
actually pretty all right.

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:00.530
It was kinda nice.

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:03.230
But, I had a job then.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:04.910
And the company hired--

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:05.880
It was a cleaning job,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.130
it was janitorial,

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:09.800
but the company that I worked for,

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.690
I guess they bid for the company again

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:12.523
or whatever,

00:04:12.523 --> 00:04:13.356
and they lost,

00:04:13.356 --> 00:04:16.440
so I was getting laid off.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:20.933
And I just went back to smoking.

00:04:24.744 --> 00:04:25.577
- (Mark) Do you ever have contact

00:04:25.577 --> 00:04:27.796
with any of your other family?

00:04:27.796 --> 00:04:28.820
- (Kellie) I do have family.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.560
I still have four brothers and a mother,

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:32.230
but my family is um...

00:04:34.317 --> 00:04:37.959
Everyone is in contact with my mom,

00:04:37.959 --> 00:04:40.840
but none of the siblings are in contact

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:41.750
with each other.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:43.700
So like, if my mom tells me

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.010
maybe my brother Damon
is doing this or that,

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.048
that's how I know what's going on.

00:04:48.048 --> 00:04:50.184
Yeah.

00:04:50.184 --> 00:04:54.578
- (Mark) So how do you spend
your day now typically?

00:04:54.578 --> 00:04:55.883
- (Kellie) Mostly just um--

00:04:55.883 --> 00:04:57.294
- (Mark) Are you using the drugs still?

00:04:57.294 --> 00:04:58.127
- (Kellie) That's it.

00:04:58.127 --> 00:04:58.960
- (Mark) Crack?

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:00.234
- (Kellie) Yes.

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:01.807
- (Mark) And how do you support yourself?

00:05:01.807 --> 00:05:03.710
- (Kellie) Wow. I do whatever I need to do

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.480
to support myself.

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:06.510
If it's have sex,

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.810
okay, that's cool.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:09.100
If it's steal something,

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.000
you know take--

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.650
if somebody's slippin'?

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:13.086
Hey, you know,

00:05:13.086 --> 00:05:15.894
that's just how it is, you know.

00:05:15.894 --> 00:05:16.727
- (Mark) Yeah.

00:05:16.727 --> 00:05:18.622
- (Kellie) So, I don't know.

00:05:18.622 --> 00:05:19.455
- (Mark) Wow.

00:05:19.455 --> 00:05:21.070
But, looking back at your life,

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:22.760
what do you think was,

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:30.648
what would've changed the
path of your life most?

00:05:30.648 --> 00:05:32.210
- (Kellie) What would've
changed the path of my life?

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:33.893
Just, I don't know,

00:05:33.893 --> 00:05:36.497
if my childhood you know,

00:05:36.497 --> 00:05:40.090
if everything would've just been different

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:43.913
because the way everything
happened is messed up.

00:05:44.813 --> 00:05:46.120
And I know it plays--

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:47.600
I got some issues about it.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.210
I really don't know all of them,

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:50.900
but some of them I know.

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:55.310
But I don't really like to
blame it on my childhood,

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:56.290
but really and truly--

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.763
because I'm an adult now,

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:02.483
so my childhood is gone, and
I'm still like, fucked up.

00:06:03.353 --> 00:06:04.620
- (Mark) Did you ever have a dad?

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:05.453
- I have a father.

00:06:05.453 --> 00:06:07.294
My father came and got
me at the age of 14.

00:06:07.294 --> 00:06:08.127
- (Mark) Oh that's right.

00:06:08.127 --> 00:06:09.278
He came out of prison, right?

00:06:09.278 --> 00:06:10.800
- Yeah, he was in federal prison,

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.270
but I guess he had been
out of federal prison,

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:14.470
and me and my grandmother,

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.320
which is his mother,

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.580
my grandmother was always like,

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:19.980
that's my grandmother.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:20.813
And um.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:25.670
Wait a minute.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:26.950
She got in touch with him,

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:28.100
'cause that's her son,

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:29.720
and I guess told him I was having a lot

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:31.077
of problems or whatever,

00:06:31.077 --> 00:06:32.243
and so he came.

00:06:33.355 --> 00:06:34.380
- (Mark) So maybe the
best years of your life

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:37.010
are those two years where you were clean?

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:39.300
- Yeah those were the most peaceful.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:41.830
I can remember that peace inside.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.021
Yeah.

00:06:43.021 --> 00:06:44.239
It was cool.

00:06:44.239 --> 00:06:45.072
- (Mark) What do you see for your future?

00:06:45.072 --> 00:06:47.460
Do you see yourself getting clean?

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.610
Getting off the street?

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.350
I mean I know you're in an SRO,

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:53.320
which is not on the street technically,

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:54.930
but you're still on skid row.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:58.700
- Um. I don't know if I'll ever get clean.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:00.080
I've been clean,

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:02.363
I've been to other programs and,

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.590
I always kinda look at it like,

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:08.763
if God works it out, then
God works it out, you know.

00:07:09.811 --> 00:07:11.061
And that's just how I go.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:15.100
- (Mark) All right, Kellie.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.718
Well thank you so much
for sharing your story.

00:07:16.718 --> 00:07:17.551
- Okay.

00:07:17.551 --> 00:07:19.820
- (Mark) And good luck with your life

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:20.860
and wherever you go from here.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:22.647
- Okay. Thank you.

